# Lines of compiler/src that no-primitive-semantics allows, one per line:
# `path: text -- reason`. Serializing a literal is not computing with it.
compiler/src/IdrisMLIR/MLIR.idr: decimal (prim__cast_DoubleString d) -- the MLIR text of a Double literal: the shortest decimal that reads back as the same bits; it computes nothing
compiler/src/IdrisMLIR/Types.idr: show (LDouble d) = prim__cast_DoubleString d -- a Double literal in the .core dump; it computes nothing
compiler/src/IdrisMLIR/Frontend/Translate/Terms.idr: LStr codegenName -- System.Info.codegen is the name this backend is registered under; the string is that name, not a value a primitive computes
